{
 "id": "fox-shield-then-punish",
 "name": "Take it on shield",
 "part": "neutral",
 "characters": [
  "fox"
 ],
 "shield": "infinite",
 "goal": "Shield an attack and punish it out of the shield; spot dodge a grab",
 "why": "Fox does not have to beat an approach: shielding it and shining out of the shield turns it into his combo. A shield does not stop a grab, though, so an opponent that runs up without attacking has to be answered another way: a spot dodge out of the shield lets the grab pass through him.",
 "switch": "success",
 "tutorial": {
  "what": "Hold L or R. Against an attack: on the first frame after shield stun, X or Y with the shield held and down-B as Fox leaves the ground. Against a grab: down on the stick as it reaches.",
  "expect": "A try begins when the opponent starts its attack or its grab and is judged when Fox hits or grabs it, when it hits or grabs him, or when it can act again. An attack has to be punished; a grab only avoided.",
  "example": [
   {
    "trigger": "R",
    "frame": -9,
    "hold": 400
   },
   {
    "press": "jump",
    "frame": "OJ",
    "from": {
     "leaves": "shield_stun"
    }
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     0,
     -1
    ],
    "frame": "OJ+J",
    "from": {
     "leaves": "shield_stun"
    }
   },
   {
    "press": "B",
    "frame": "OJ+J",
    "from": {
     "leaves": "shield_stun"
    }
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     0,
     -1
    ],
    "frame": "SD",
    "hold": 2,
    "from": "start"
   }
  ],
  "marks": {
   "1": "Frame 1: its attack starts. Keep the shield up"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "The attack on the shield",
    "text": [
     "{opp} plays footsies and then commits. An attack on Fox's shield leaves it in lag; Fox leaves shield stun and can jump out of the shield at once.",
     "X or Y with the shield held, and down-B on the first frame in the air: the shine hits {4} frames after shield stun, before the attacker can act."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "trigger": "R",
        "frame": -9,
        "hold": 400
       },
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": "OJ",
        "from": {
         "leaves": "shield_stun"
        }
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": "OJ+J",
        "from": {
         "leaves": "shield_stun"
        }
       },
       {
        "press": "B",
        "frame": "OJ+J",
        "from": {
         "leaves": "shield_stun"
        }
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": "SD",
        "hold": 2,
        "from": "start"
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: its attack starts. Keep the shield up"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "The grab",
    "text": [
     "A grab goes through a shield. When {opp} runs up without attacking, the shield is the wrong answer.",
     "Down on the stick in the shield is a spot dodge: the grab passes through Fox. From close by its whiff can be punished; from the edge of its reach, not being grabbed is the win."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "trigger": "R",
        "frame": -9,
        "hold": 400
       },
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": "OJ",
        "from": {
         "leaves": "shield_stun"
        }
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": "OJ+J",
        "from": {
         "leaves": "shield_stun"
        }
       },
       {
        "press": "B",
        "frame": "OJ+J",
        "from": {
         "leaves": "shield_stun"
        }
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": "SD",
        "hold": 2,
        "from": "start"
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: it reaches for a grab. Down on the stick: a spot dodge",
       "8": "Frame {f}: the grab passes through Fox"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  ]
 },
